 "notes": "Fig. 3 left panel of arXiv:2002.05165: 95% CL COBE/FIRAS gamma->A' constraint on kinetic mixing epsilon vs dark photon mass, extracted from the vector paths of the e-print figure limit.pdf (axis calibration residual <0.001 decades). The paper shows two PDF choices (log-normal and analytic); per the caption the shaded excluded region is bounded by the more conservative of the two, which is the log-normal curve everywhere (verified against the shaded fill path; the two curves coincide for m_A' > ~3.4e-12 eV). Reported curve = log-normal/conservative boundary, clipped to the displayed plot window (first point interpolated on the steep low-mass wall at eps = 0.1 near m_A' ~ 1.9e-15 eV; curve ends at the axis edge m_A' = 1e-9 eV). This limit is from CMB spectral distortions and does not assume dark photon dark matter (hence dm_density_assumed null); the paper's separate DPDM heating limit (Fig. 3 right) is not reported. PIXIE and Dark SRF curves in the same figure are projections and were excluded.",
